I nearly always genocide liches first, followed by eels, in a game
which I think I have a reasonable chance of winning.  If I'm a
low-level character without great stats, however, I might genocide
nymphs or mumakil first.  In either case I would also get rid of rust
monsters fairly quickly - just being able to remove a ball of
punishment isn't much of a reason to keep something around (ditto for
nymphs).  I rarely read scrolls before I identify them anyway, unless I
know they're blessed.

I would NEVER genocide wraiths.  If you have Excalibur, you can't be
level-drained, and in any case you get the level back when you kill the
monster (although you start down at the beginning of that level). 
Remember you can keep gaining experience and HP after level 30. 
Vampires on the other hand I get rid of because you can't eat them to
gain levels.

Eels are of absolutely no use IMO.  I would genocide them even earlier
than liches except that eels are easier to avoid (as they can't leave
the water unless, so I hear, it's frozen).  Dwarves aren't really worth
genociding, although more than a few have made short work of me with
their damn heavy picks.  Rock moles can mess up the map all they want
as far as I'm concerned - more rocks to polypile (unless you're worried
about golems).  Gelatinous cubes can do nasty things but they grant
LOTS of intrinsics, so they're worth keeping around for awhile.

Dragons I would get rid of only if you have all of the intrinsics AND
you have either genocided gremlins or you have lots of tins of the
appropriate intrinsic-granting foods (and that's not even foolproof as
you only get a percentage-chance with most things).  There are very few
intrinsics that I'd actually WANT to get rid of, although having
teleport without teleport control is very annoying, and I've heard the
Caveman's quest item gives you intrinsic conflict, which could be quite
a problem.  Don't get rid of giants until you've maxed out your
strength, which may take awhile (though of course you can get bonuses
from beehives and giant zombies too).

In my latest game I believe I got rid of L;RDHcnV (not necessarily in
that order).  Ended up being some 37 species with all of the variations
on each letter.  Very helpful - got through hell and back (literally)
without much trouble from anything but the Wiz.  But then again, I
usually don't find or polypile 12-15 magic markers. :)

